invariant: INV-14
file: handshake_parser.c
catches: handshake_strict_webpki
reason: the ALPN arm stops checking that the extension ends at the one
  ProtocolName, so bytes after it parse instead of failing. RFC 9846
  §4.3 makes extension_data match its structure exactly, and a reader
  that ignores the remainder is where a smuggled second name would sit.
  bin/handshake_strict_webpki's trailing-byte row objects.

--- old
    if (e.err || name_len == 0 || list_len != 1 + name_len || rb_left(&e) != 0) {
--- new
    if (e.err || name_len == 0 || list_len != 1 + name_len) {
